+# Pre-ship review — USDC Payouts dApp (Base)
+
+Scope: `packages/nextjs` frontend + config, plus deploy/verify posture. Static review; the app could not be run locally (`node_modules` state file missing, `yarn next:check-types` fails to start).
+
+Paths are relative to repo root. Severity: **ship-blocking** = do not ship to real users as-is; **should-fix** = ship risk / quality debt.
+
+---
+
+## Ship-blocking
+
+### 1. Disconnected users get a paragraph, not a Connect button
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:70-71`
+
+`{!isConnected ? <p>Please connect your wallet to send a payout.</p> : ...}`. Dead end — the user has to hunt for the header button.
+
+**Fix:** render the connect button in the action slot.
+```tsx
+import { RainbowKitCustomConnectButton } from "~~/components/scaffold-eth";
+// ...
+if (!isConnected) return <RainbowKitCustomConnectButton />;
+```
+
+### 2. No wrong-network branch on the primary CTA
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:99-114`
+
+Only the header has `WrongNetworkDropdown`. A wallet on Ethereum/Optimism sees live Approve/Send Payout buttons; clicking signs against the wrong chain or fails silently.
+
+**Fix:** gate the action slot on `chain.id !== targetNetwork.id` and render a switch button instead:
+```tsx
+const { chain } = useAccount();
+const { targetNetwork } = useTargetNetwork();
+const { switchChain } = useSwitchChain();
+// ...
+if (chain?.id !== targetNetwork.id)
+  return (
+    <button className="btn btn-primary" onClick={() => switchChain?.({ chainId: targetNetwork.id })}>
+      Switch to {targetNetwork.name}
+    </button>
+  );
+```
+
+### 3. Writes use raw wagmi `useWriteContract`
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:6, 21, 38-43, 51-56`
+
+Bypasses everything `useScaffoldWriteContract` provides: pre-flight simulation, the wrong-network guard, the tx-progress notifications, and — critically — resolution at *confirmation* rather than at wallet signature. `setAmount("")` on line 57 runs the moment the wallet returns a hash, so the form clears while the tx is still pending and may still revert.
+
+**Fix:** two hook instances, one per contract.
+```tsx
+const { writeContractAsync: writeUsdc, isMining: isApproving } = useScaffoldWriteContract({ contractName: "USDC" });
+const { writeContractAsync: writePayouts, isMining: isPaying } = useScaffoldWriteContract({ contractName: "Payouts" });
+
+await writePayouts({ functionName: "pay", args: [recipient, parseUnits(amount, 6), memo] });
+```
+Drop the manual `address`/`abi` args and the `deployedContracts` import (see #6).
+
+### 4. Failed and rejected transactions fail silently
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:44-46, 59-61`
+
+Both `catch` blocks only `console.error(e)`. A user who rejects in their wallet, or whose `transferFrom` reverts for insufficient allowance, sees the button re-enable and nothing else.
+
+**Fix:** surface it.
+```tsx
+} catch (e) {
+  notification.error(getParsedError(e));
+}
+```
+(`import { notification, getParsedError } from "~~/utils/scaffold-eth";`) Switching to `useScaffoldWriteContract` per #3 covers most of this automatically; keep the `catch` for the rest.
+
+### 5. Buttons unlock mid-flight (`isPending`, not `isMining`)
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:21, 101-110`
+
+`isPending` from wagmi drops as soon as the wallet hands back a tx hash — before the receipt. The user gets a live "Send Payout" button while the previous payout is still confirming, and can double-send.
+
+**Fix:** lock on `isMining` from `useScaffoldWriteContract`, which is held across `waitForTransactionReceipt` and cleared in the hook's `finally` on both confirmation and rejection. If you add a post-confirmation allowance/balance refetch, hold it in local state and clear it in `finally` too — never on a timer.
+
+### 6. USDC is hand-added to `deployedContracts.ts`
+`packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts:50-...` (and consumed at `app/payouts/page.tsx:10-11`)
+
+That file is regenerated by `generateTsAbis` on every `yarn deploy` (`packages/hardhat/hardhat.config.ts:19-28`), and the only deploy script deploys `Payouts` (`packages/hardhat/deploy/00_deploy_payouts.ts`). The next deploy wipes the USDC entry — `useScaffoldReadContract({ contractName: "USDC" })` silently returns nothing, and `deployedContracts[8453].USDC` becomes a type error that breaks the build.
+
+**Fix:** move it to the file meant for it.
+```typescript
+// packages/nextjs/contracts/externalContracts.ts
+const externalContracts = {
+  8453: {
+    USDC: { address: "0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913", abi: [...] },
+  },
+} as const;
+
+export default externalContracts satisfies GenericContractsDeclaration;
+```
+Then revert `deployedContracts.ts` to its generated state and confirm `yarn next:check-types` passes. While you're there, drop the `deployedContracts[8453]` imports on the page — hardcoding chain `8453` at module scope breaks the moment `targetNetworks` changes; the scaffold hooks resolve address + ABI from the target network for you.
+
+### 7. Hardcoded dark wrapper on the page root
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:65`
+
+`className="min-h-screen bg-black text-white"` bypasses DaisyUI entirely. Light-mode users get a black page, the footer's `SwitchTheme` becomes a no-op on this route, and `border-gray-700` (line 121) is invisible on light backgrounds.
+
+**Fix:** `className="min-h-screen bg-base-200 text-base-content"`, and swap `border-gray-700` for `border-base-300`. (Forcing `data-theme="dark"` would be acceptable only if `<SwitchTheme/>` were removed — it isn't.)
+
+### 8. Approve and Send Payout are both live; allowance is never read
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:99-114`
+
+Nothing reads USDC allowance, so both buttons render at once with no ordering. A first-time user clicks "Send Payout", `transferFrom` reverts, and per #4 they see nothing. Conversely a user who already has allowance is still shown a pointless Approve.
+
+**Fix:** read allowance and let it pick the button.
+```tsx
+const { data: allowance } = useScaffoldReadContract({
+  contractName: "USDC",
+  functionName: "allowance",
+  args: [connectedAddress, payoutsAddress],
+});
+const needsApproval = allowance !== undefined && allowance < parseUnits(amount || "0", 6);
+```
+Render Approve when `needsApproval`, Send Payout otherwise — one primary action at a time (Connect → Switch → Approve → Pay). This also removes the current stale-allowance trap, where approving for one amount and then editing the field leaves an approval that no longer covers the payout.
+
+### 9. Recipient is a raw `<input type="text">`
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:78-84`
+
+No ENS resolution, no checksum validation. `vitalik.eth` is passed to the contract as-is via the `recipient as \`0x${string}\`` cast on line 55 and reverts; a typo'd address sends USDC into the void.
+
+**Fix:**
+```tsx
+import { AddressInput } from "@scaffold-ui/components";
+<AddressInput value={recipient} onChange={setRecipient} placeholder="Recipient address or ENS" />
+```
+Also consider `IntegerInput`/a decimal-aware input for the amount — `type="number"` currently accepts negatives and >6-decimal values.
+
+### 10. Event history scans Base mainnet from block 0
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:29-34`
+
+`fromBlock: 0n` with `watch: true` on a chain currently ~34M blocks deep. `useScaffoldEventHistory` paginates forward from `fromBlock` in a `fetchNextPage` loop, so this fires thousands of `eth_getLogs` calls — the feed effectively never loads and the RPC key gets rate-limited or banned.
+
+**Fix:** drop `fromBlock` entirely. The hook defaults to `deployedOnBlock` from `deployedContracts.ts` (`33712450`), which is exactly right. If you keep it explicit, use `33712450n`.
+
+### 11. Production ships on the shared default RPC key
+`packages/nextjs/scaffold.config.ts:16, 29, 32-35`
+
+`alchemyApiKey` falls back to `DEFAULT_ALCHEMY_API_KEY` (the public SE-2 demo key) and `rpcOverrides` is empty, so with no `NEXT_PUBLIC_ALCHEMY_API_KEY` set the app runs on a shared, rate-limited key — and `wagmiConfig.tsx:20` deprioritizes it behind the bare `http()` public-endpoint fallback when the default key is detected. There is no `.env.local` in `packages/nextjs`; only `.env.example`.
+
+**Fix:** provision a dedicated key (or a Base RPC provider) and route it through `rpcOverrides`:
+```typescript
+rpcOverrides: {
+  [chains.base.id]: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_RPC_URL as string,
+},
+```
+Add the variable to `.env.example` and **verify it is actually set in the Vercel project env**, not just referenced in code.
+
+---
+
+## Should-fix
+
+### 12. `pollingInterval: 30000` on an L2
+`packages/nextjs/scaffold.config.ts:24`
+
+30s on Base (2s blocks) makes the balance and the payouts feed feel broken — a confirmed payout takes up to half a minute to appear.
+
+**Fix:** set `pollingInterval: 3000`, and additionally refetch balance/allowance on the `onBlockConfirmation` callback of the pay write so the UI updates immediately rather than on the next poll.
+
+### 13. Default WalletConnect project ID
+`packages/nextjs/scaffold.config.ts:40`
+
+Falls back to the shared SE-2 demo project ID. Shared quota, and no control over the app metadata shown in wallets during connection.
+
+**Fix:** register a project at cloud.reown.com, set `NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLET_CONNECT_PROJECT_ID` in the host env, and set `appName` in `services/web3/wagmiConnectors.tsx:49` to the product name (currently `"scaffold-eth-2"` — this string is what users see in their wallet's connection prompt).
+
+### 14. Pill-shaped inputs from `--radius-field: 9999rem`
+`packages/nextjs/styles/globals.css:36` and `:63`
+
+Both the light and dark theme blocks set it. The recipient/amount inputs and the memo textarea render as capsules that clip long addresses.
+
+**Fix:** set `--radius-field: 0.5rem;` in **both** `@plugin "daisyui/theme"` blocks — at theme level, not with per-component `rounded-*` overrides.
+
+### 15. DaisyUI `loading` class on the buttons swallows the label
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:101, 108`
+
+`btn ${isPending ? "loading" : ""}` replaces the entire button content with a spinner — mid-transaction the user sees two anonymous spinners with no idea which action is running.
+
+**Fix:** keep the label, add an inline spinner.
+```tsx
+<button className="btn btn-primary" disabled={isMining} onClick={handleApprove}>
+  {isMining && <span className="loading loading-spinner loading-sm" />}
+  Approve
+</button>
+```
+
+### 16. Addresses rendered with a hand-rolled `shorten()`
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:13, 122, 124`
+
+No blockie, no ENS name, no copy button, no explorer link — and in a payouts feed, "who got paid" is the whole point.
+
+**Fix:** `import { Address } from "@scaffold-ui/components";` and render `<Address address={payout.args.from} />` / `<Address address={payout.args.to} />`. Delete `shorten`.
+
+### 17. The Payouts contract itself is never shown
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx`
+
+The page shows the user's balance but never the contract they're approving and sending USDC through. Users are asked to grant an ERC-20 allowance to an address they can't see or verify.
+
+**Fix:** render the address next to the approve step, with a link to Basescan:
+```tsx
+<div className="text-sm">Payouts contract: <Address address={payoutsAddress} /></div>
+```
+
+### 18. Phantom users cannot connect
+`packages/nextjs/services/web3/wagmiConnectors.tsx:2-9, 20-28`
+
+Phantom is not in RainbowKit's default list and is not added here. A significant share of Base users have Phantom as their only wallet and simply cannot use the app.
+
+**Fix:**
+```tsx
+import { phantomWallet } from "@rainbow-me/rainbowkit/wallets";
+const wallets = [metaMaskWallet, walletConnectWallet, phantomWallet, ledgerWallet, baseAccount, rainbowWallet, safeWallet, ...];
+```
+
+### 19. No mobile deep-link back to the wallet after a write
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:36-62`
+
+On a phone connected over WalletConnect, tapping Approve or Send Payout fires the request but leaves the user on the page — nothing happens visually and they have to find their wallet app by hand to sign. This is the single biggest mobile drop-off point.
+
+**Fix:** after firing the write (never before — navigating away first means the write never runs), redirect to the wallet the user actually connected with, and skip it inside a wallet's in-app browser:
+```tsx
+const { connector } = useAccount();
+const promise = writePayouts({ ... });          // fire first
+if (isMobile && !isInWalletBrowser) redirectToWallet(connector);
+await promise;
+```
+Test this on a real device before ship.
+
+### 20. Scaffold-ETH branding still throughout
+Five places, all still template defaults:
+
+- `packages/nextjs/app/layout.tsx:11-12` — tab title `"Scaffold-ETH 2 App"`, description `"Built with 🏗 Scaffold-ETH 2"`. Also `utils/scaffold-eth/getMetadata.ts:8` — every page title is templated as `"%s | Scaffold-ETH 2"`.
+- `packages/nextjs/components/Footer.tsx:50-74` — "Fork me" → the SE-2 repo, "Built with ♥ at BuidlGuidl", and a Support link to the SE-2 Telegram. Real users clicking Support land in a stranger's group chat.
+- `packages/nextjs/app/page.tsx:22, 30-45` — the home page is still the untouched template ("Welcome to Scaffold-ETH 2", "Get started by editing page.tsx", "Edit your smart contract YourContract.sol"). It's the first thing a real user sees.
+- `README.md` — the stock SE-2 readme.
+- `packages/nextjs/public/favicon.png`, `logo.svg`, `thumbnail.jpg` — stock SE-2 assets; the thumbnail is what renders when someone shares a payout link.
+
+**Fix:** replace all five with product copy and assets. Separately, `packages/nextjs/public/manifest.json` is **not valid JSON** — unquoted keys and single quotes (`{ name: 'Scaffold-ETH 2 DApp', ... }`) — so it fails to parse for anything that reads it. Rewrite it as valid JSON with the product name, or delete it if unused (nothing currently references it).
+
+### 21. Contract verification not done
+`packages/hardhat/` has no `deployments/` directory
+
+The Payouts address in `deployedContracts.ts` (`0x7c3f2A9d41B85E60Cf14a14e2b9D073A55e0b6F2`) has a `deployedOnBlock`, but there are no deployment artifacts in the repo, so `yarn verify --network base` has nothing to submit and was almost certainly never run. Unverified bytecode on a contract users grant USDC allowance to reads as something to hide.
+
+**Fix:** confirm the address on Basescan; if the source isn't published, redeploy-or-verify with the original artifacts and run `yarn verify --network base`. Commit `packages/hardhat/deployments/` so this is reproducible.
+
+### 22. Shared default Etherscan API key
+`packages/hardhat/hardhat.config.ts:17`
+
+`ETHERSCAN_API_KEY` falls back to a hardcoded shared key. Verification will intermittently fail on rate limits.
+
+**Fix:** set `ETHERSCAN_API_KEY` in `packages/hardhat/.env` and drop the fallback (or let it fail loudly).
+
+### 23. Feed shows "No payouts yet" while still loading
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:120, 130`
+
+`payouts` is `undefined` during the initial fetch, so the empty state renders immediately and then flips to a populated list — it reads as "your payout didn't go through".
+
+**Fix:** destructure `isLoading` from `useScaffoldEventHistory` and render a skeleton (`<div className="skeleton h-16 w-full" />`) while loading; show the empty state only when `!isLoading && payouts?.length === 0`.
+
+### 24. Event list keyed by array index
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:120-121`
+
+With `watch: true`, new events are **prepended** (`useScaffoldEventHistory.ts:246`), so every existing row's index shifts and React remounts the whole list on each new payout.
+
+**Fix:** `key={`${payout.transactionHash}-${payout.logIndex}`}`.
+
+### 25. Balance doesn't refresh after a payout
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:23-27`
+
+`usdcBalance` has no `watch` and nothing refetches it after a successful pay, so the displayed balance stays stale until a remount.
+
+**Fix:** call the read hook's `refetch` (along with the allowance refetch from #8) in the pay handler's `onBlockConfirmation`, holding the button disabled until it resolves.
+
+---
+
+## Notes
+
+- `yarn next:check-types` and a local run were not possible — dependencies aren't installed in this workspace. Please run both after applying #6 in particular; that one is expected to surface type errors either way.
+- `next.config.ts:7-9` allows `NEXT_PUBLIC_IGNORE_BUILD_ERROR=true` to skip TypeScript errors at build. Make sure that variable is **not** set in the Vercel project.

